Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Dropout Recovery for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing
Version: 0.7.0
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects high-confidence technical zero events in single-cell RNA-seq
    data using SuperCell-style local memberships, low-rank reconstruction, and
    finite-sample empirical-Bayes zero-null testing with gene-wise false-discovery
    control. Recovery engines can use memberships as either hard local blocks or
    soft biological priors. The soft barycentric engine learns target-independent
    donor weights from the biological embedding while combining SuperCell hierarchy
    and membership information, then selectively borrows positive target-gene
    expression from biologically similar cells. Predictive uncertainty is retained
    and observed non-dropout values are never overwritten.
